// example.readme-present — the first ordinary CM to execute end to end.
//
// Governing question: does the subject repository present a README at its root?
//
// This is deliberately the smallest useful methodology: one leaf that
// terminates at a single primitive mechanical provider (`file.exists`). It
// exists to prove the runtime path — compile-time contract, link, execute a
// real provider, capture evidence, emit a receipt — not to say anything deep
// about repositories.
//
// NOTE ON STATUS: the executed artifact is the hand-authored NormalizedCMIR in
// `ir/readme-present.ir.json`, exactly as the Ascent-0 runtime consumes a
// hand-authored IR today. This `.cm` records author intent; the surface
// compiler does not yet emit this IR, nor does it yet lower the `decide` block
// (the runtime carries that decision projection for this one CM). When
// `coh cm compile` can lower a leaf of this shape, this file becomes the source
// and the IR becomes a build output.

methodology "example.readme-present" version "0.1" {
  subject repository as target_root

  measure readme_presence
    by file.exists { relative_path = "README.md" } over target_root

  decide
    | README_PRESENT when readme_presence
    | README_ABSENT  otherwise
}
